-------\nAPPENDICES 362 (https://theses.ncl.ac.uk/jspui/bitstream/10443/1757/1/Kim%2099.pdf)\nciteturn54search17 [wordlim: 200] Published: 13.3 years ago; Crawled: 13.3 years ago; Tryptone-yeast extract broth (ISP medium 1; Shirling & Gottlieb, 1966)\n\nBacto-tryptone (Difco), 5.0 g; Bacto-yeast extract (Difco), 3.0 g; distilled water, 1 litre; pH 7.0-7.2.\nAPPENDICES 362\n\nResistance to lysozyme (Gordon & Barnett, 1977)\n\nA solution, made by dissolving 0.1 g lysozyme in 100 ml of sterile distilled water in a volumetric flask, sterilised by filtration using a disposable filter (0.45 µm; Acrodisc, Gelman Sciences, 600 South Wagner Road, Ann Arbor, Michigan, USA). This stock solution was stored at 3 to 4 °C for up to 2 weeks. A 5ml amount of the stock lysozyme solution was mixed with 95 ml of sterile glycerol broth (Lab M peptone, 5.0 g; Lab Lemco, 2.4 g; glycerol 70 ml; distilled water, 1litre, pH 7.0) and dispensed aseptically into sterile capped tubes. Tubes of lysozyme (300 to 500 U/ml) and glycerol broth (control) were seeded with a small amount of inoculum taken from plates incubated for less than 7 days. The cultures were observed for growth after a week of incubation at 45 °C.\n\nSauton’s broth, modified (Mordarska et al., 1972)\n\nL-asparagine, 5.0 g; casamino acid, 2.0 g; glucose, 15 g; sodium citrate, 5.0 g; potassium dihydrogen phosphate, 5.0 g; magnesium sulphate, 0.5 g; potassium sulphate, 0.5 g; ferric ammonium citrate, trace; distilled water, 1 litre; pH 7.2. The medium and glucose were autoclaved separately at 121 °C for 20 minutes.\n\nTrace salts solution (Pridham & Gottlieb, 1966)\n\nFeSO4.7H2O, 0.1 g; MnCl2.4H2O, 0.1 g; ZnSO4.7H2O, 0.1 g; distilled water, 100 ml. Use as directed in ISP media 3, 4, 5 and 7.\n\nTryptic soy agar (Difco)\n\nBacto-tryptone, 15 g; Bacto-soytone, 5 g; NaCl, 5 g; Bacto-agar, 15 g; distilled water, 1 litre; pH 7.2. Autoclave at 121 °C for 20 minutes.\n\nTryptone-yeast extract broth (ISP medium 1; Shirling & Gottlieb, 1966)\n\nBacto-tryptone (Difco), 5.0 g; Bacto-yeast extract (Difco), 3.0 g; distilled water, 1 litre; pH 7.0-7.2. Autoclave at 121 °C for 20 minutes.\n\nTyrosine agar (ISP medium 7; Shirling & Gottlieb, 1966)\n\nGlycerol, 15 g; L-tyrosine, 0.5 g; L-asparagine, 1.0 g; K2HPO4 (anhydrous--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMain sol. J656 | Solutions | MediaDive (https://bacmedia.dsmz.de/solutions/4543)\nciteturn54search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; (BD-Difco)  | 5  | g  | 5  | 70.343 ... 2 Comment: The premixed powder of Tryptone-yeast extract broth is available from Becton Dickinson & Co. as ISP Medium 1.\n\n# Main sol. J656\n\nDownload this solution as\n\nCSV JSON PDF\n\nInternal Solution-ID: S4543\n\nCompound  | Amount  | Unit  | Conc. [g/L]  | Conc. [mM]\n--- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nTryptone\n(BD-Difco)  | 5  | g  | 5  | 70.343\nYeast extract\n(BD-Difco)  | 3  | g  | 3  | -\nMgSO_{4} x 7 H_{2}O  | 2  | g  | 2  | 8.114\nDistilled water  | 1000  | ml  | -  | -\n1 Adjust pH to 7.0 - 7.2.\n2 Comment: The premixed powder of Tryptone-yeast extract broth is available from Becton Dickinson & Co. as ISP Medium 1. Add MgSO_{4} x 7H2O to the medium before autoclaving.\n\n#### Media with this solution\n\nJ656  | TRYPTONE-YEAST EXTRACT BROTH (ISP-1) WITH 0.2% MgSO_{4}·7H_{2}O--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nJ656: TRYPTONE-YEAST EXTRACT BROTH (ISP-1) WITH 0.2% MgSO<sub>4</sub>·7H<sub>2</sub>O | Media | MediaDive (https://bacmedia.dsmz.de/medium/J656)\nciteturn54search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; (BD-Difco)  | 5  | g  | 5  | 70.343 ... 2 Comment: The premixed powder of Tryptone-yeast extract broth is available from Becton Dickinson & Co. as ISP Medium 1.\n\n# Image: JCM Medium 656 . TRYPTONE-YEAST EXTRACT BROTH (ISP-1) WITH 0.2% MgSO_{4}·7H_{2}O\n\nInofficial medium: This medium was provided by external sources and is possibly not curated by experts.\n\n##### Valid